From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Subtitles: turn the realignment of a file on or off while it
 plays

Whether a subtitle file beside the video is realigned was a setting,
read when the file opens. A viewer who sees it go wrong for one film, or
wants it for one film only, had to leave playback to change it.

PlayerControl(SubtitleRealign) now turns it the other way for the
playing video, and VideoPlayer.SubtitleRealign tells a skin which way it
is. Turned off, the file's lines go back to their own times at once and
the video is no longer read; turned on, they are realigned - on what was
found for this file before, if anything, else read again. The choice
holds for the video while it plays, through picking another subtitle
and back; another video starts again from the setting. A choice made
before any file is open is the next file's.

The info label takes the id 415 Kodi leaves unused, and the built-in is
a PlayerControl parameter, so neither moves the numbering of Kodi's own.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
